a babysitter accused of killing a child  remains in jail tonight a lot of viewers  responded after the i-team first broke  the story back in march  vanessa murphy continues to follow the  criminal case and also has more about  what unfolded in court this morning  now we do want to warn you the details  in the story are of a disturbing nature  lauren courtney appeared in a courtroom  here at the regional justice center  metro police say she beat a child to  death while  babysitting him and it was caught on  video  lauren courtney  22-year-old lauren courtney faces murder  and child abuse charges  a prosecutor saying in court tuesday  she's now received  autopsy results for five-year-old ryan  james peralta  which could result in amended charges  the child died on march  12. according to this arrest report  courtney told police  she babysat for ryan and his  seven-year-old sister since  august ryan's father had installed  cameras in his home  after his daughter said courtney hurt  ryan while at work  he received a call from courtney that  ryan wasn't doing well and he was  coughing up blood ryan's dad returned  home to find his son  unresponsive on the couch detectives say  courtney was angry the child  urinated on himself and she is seen on  video  dragging ryan while he was limp kicking  him in the head  dropping him so his head hit the  bathroom floor  punching him in the face and dragging  him into the shower  the report states she turns the water on  as ryan cries and moans in pain  during an interview with police  detectives describe  courtney as showing no emotion and say  she claimed she has mental health issues  she's expected to be back in court on  august 12th  i asked courtney's lawyer if she'd like  to send a statement  on her behalf and she declined reporting  in downtown las vegas vanessa murphy 8  news now
 

